{"id": "SATM29KVA0M", "skill_codes": ["Linear Equations in Two Variables"], "difficulty": 1, "stem": "Which of the following ordered pairs \\((x, y)\\) satisfies the equation \\(4x - 3y = 22\\)?", "options": [{"key": "A", "text": "\\((2, 7)\\)"}, {"key": "B", "text": "\\((4, 2)\\)"}, {"key": "C", "text": "\\((7, 2)\\)"}, {"key": "D", "text": "\\((7, -2)\\)"}], "correct_answer": "C", "explanation": "Substituting \\(x = 7\\) and \\(y = 2\\) gives \\(4(7) - 3(2) = 28 - 6 = 22\\), which matches the right side. The pair \\((2, 7)\\) gives \\(8 - 21 = -13\\), not 22. The pair \\((4, 2)\\) gives \\(16 - 6 = 10\\), not 22. The pair \\((7, -2)\\) gives \\(28 + 6 = 34\\), not 22, resulting from a sign error in substitution."}
{"id": "SATM29MKN22", "skill_codes": ["Linear Equations in Two Variables"], "difficulty": 1, "stem": "A line passes through the points $(1, 5)$ and $(4, 17)$. What is the $y$-intercept of this line?", "options": [{"key": "A", "text": "$(0, 1)$"}, {"key": "B", "text": "$(0, -1)$"}, {"key": "C", "text": "$(0, 4)$"}, {"key": "D", "text": "$(0, 5)$"}], "correct_answer": "A", "explanation": "The slope is $m = \\frac{17 - 5}{4 - 1} = \\frac{12}{3} = 4$. Using point-slope with $(1, 5)$: $y - 5 = 4(x - 1)$, so $y = 4x + 1$. The $y$-intercept is $(0, 1)$. The value $(0, -1)$ is a sign error when computing $5 - 4 = 1$. The value $(0, 4)$ confuses the slope with the intercept. The value $(0, 5)$ uses the $y$-coordinate of the first point without adjustment."}
{"id": "SATM29Y1LJ0", "skill_codes": ["Linear Equations in Two Variables"], "difficulty": 2, "stem": "A line passes through the points $(1, 5)$ and $(3, 11)$. What is the $y$-intercept of this line?", "options": [], "correct_answer": "2", "explanation": "The slope of the line is $\\frac{11 - 5}{3 - 1} = \\frac{6}{2} = 3$. Using point-slope form with the point $(1, 5)$: $y - 5 = 3(x - 1)$, which simplifies to $y = 3x + 2$. The $y$-intercept is $2$."}
{"id": "SATM2A4R46G", "skill_codes": ["Linear Equations in Two Variables"], "difficulty": 2, "stem": "What is the slope of the line that passes through the points $(7, -19)$ and $(-5, 29)$?", "options": [{"key": "A", "text": "$-4$"}, {"key": "B", "text": "$-\\frac{1}{4}$"}, {"key": "C", "text": "$\\frac{1}{4}$"}, {"key": "D", "text": "$4$"}], "correct_answer": "A", "explanation": "The slope formula gives $m = \\frac{29 - (-19)}{-5 - 7} = \\frac{48}{-12} = -4$. The value $-\\frac{1}{4}$ results from inverting the fraction, computing the change in $x$ over the change in $y$ instead of rise over run. The value $\\frac{1}{4}$ compounds the inversion error with a sign error, losing the negative. The value $4$ results from dropping the negative sign from the correct calculation."}
