{"id": "SATM2D3UY34", "skill_codes": ["Linear Equations in Two Variables"], "difficulty": 3, "stem": "A line passes through the points $(1, -2)$ and $(5, k)$ and is parallel to the line $5x - 2y = 10$. What is the value of $k$?", "options": [{"key": "A", "text": "$-\\frac{2}{5}$"}, {"key": "B", "text": "$8$"}, {"key": "C", "text": "$9$"}, {"key": "D", "text": "$12$"}], "correct_answer": "B", "explanation": "The correct answer is $8$. Rewriting $5x - 2y = 10$ gives $y = \\frac{5}{2}x - 5$, so parallel lines have slope $\\frac{5}{2}$. Setting the slope between the two points equal to $\\frac{5}{2}$: $\\frac{k - (-2)}{5 - 1} = \\frac{5}{2}$, so $\\frac{k + 2}{4} = \\frac{5}{2}$, giving $k + 2 = 10$ and $k = 8$. Choosing $-\\frac{2}{5}$ results from a conceptual gap: using the reciprocal slope $\\frac{2}{5}$ instead of $\\frac{5}{2}$. $9$ results from an arithmetic slip when cross-multiplying, multiplying only the $k$ term by 2 instead of the whole expression $(k+2)$. $12$ results from a sign error that treats the numerator as $k - 2$ instead of $k + 2$."}
{"id": "SATM2D6WYVE", "skill_codes": ["Linear Equations in Two Variables"], "difficulty": 3, "stem": "Line $p$ has the equation $5x - 8y = 24$. Line $q$ is perpendicular to line $p$ and passes through the point $(3, -1)$. What is the $y$-intercept of line $q$?", "options": [{"key": "A", "text": "$\\frac{19}{5}$"}, {"key": "B", "text": "$\\frac{1}{5}$"}, {"key": "C", "text": "$-\\frac{19}{5}$"}, {"key": "D", "text": "$\\frac{29}{5}$"}], "correct_answer": "A", "explanation": "Rewriting line $p$ in slope-intercept form: $-8y = -5x + 24$, so $y = \\frac{5}{8}x - 3$, giving slope $\\frac{5}{8}$. The perpendicular slope is $-\\frac{8}{5}$. Using point-slope form with $(3, -1)$: $y - (-1) = -\\frac{8}{5}(x - 3)$, which gives $y + 1 = -\\frac{8}{5}x + \\frac{24}{5}$. So $y = -\\frac{8}{5}x + \\frac{24}{5} - 1 = -\\frac{8}{5}x + \\frac{19}{5}$. The $y$-intercept is $\\frac{19}{5}$. The value $\\frac{1}{5}$ comes from an arithmetic slip when subtracting 1 from $\\frac{24}{5}$, computing $\\frac{24 - 23}{5}$ erroneously. The value $-\\frac{19}{5}$ results from a sign error when handling the perpendicular slope or the point substitution. The value $\\frac{29}{5}$ comes from incorrectly adding 1 to $\\frac{24}{5}$ instead of subtracting."}
